A||N||5||DreXteR||What do you think of this cam??||||1||
Z||000000||DreXteR||05-23-2001||12:16 AM||||I will run a turbo setup + manyu mods. <BR>This cam can be used?<BR>The specs. are: Adv. Duration: 280-290 0.050" Duration: 214-224 lift: 0.443", 0.465" Lobe Center Angle: 112<P>How it compare to the crane 2030??<P>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||05-23-2001||07:37 AM||||If that's the cam I think it is, you have the lift measured at the valve, and the duration measured at the cam. If so, that's the cam I have. It's a great cam, but it's a carb profile, and not made for fuel injection. The ramp on a fuel injection cam is more gradual than this one, with a flatter lobe peak. I know the performance difference firsthand, since I had it in with F/I, and it runs a bunch better since going with a carb. If you use that cam anyway(again, assuming it's the one I have) balance the motor, and install heavy springs. This cam has just a little bit too much headroom for the motor. I thought I could get by with stock springs, but the valves float at around 5500 RPM, and that's just at the peak of the power curve. So I'm missing the last 500-1,000 RPM of the engine's capability. Still, all in all, I'm very happy with the cars performance.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Will||05-23-2001||08:53 AM||||You might want a wider lobe separation for a turbo setup.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-23-2001||11:44 AM||||Here is what I think. The Wolverine Blue racer camshaft you are contemplating using is not a good choice if you plan on using the stock heads, tuned port injection, and your reline on your engine is only 6000 rpm. That camshaft isn't matched to the long runners of the fiero’s tuned port injection. If you plan on running this motor NA for a while than a compression ratio of 8.5 is to low for that camshaft. It is not a good street cam either because you won’t have much low-end torque. You also may not pass emissions because of the valve overlap. Because of the valve overlap your vacuum may be to low for the computerized fuel injection and it will idle rich and crappy.  <P>By comparison the Crane 2030 will make more low-end torque and horsepower and is better matched to the induction system you have. The Crane 2030 will have good street ability too. The Crane 2030 is better matched to the gear ratios you have, works with the computer, and if you have an automatic will work with that too. <P>I tested these camshafts for you in Dyno2000 and Dragstrip2000 and here is what I got NA and then using an Air Research T03 turbocharger with 10 psi of boost. I assumed you have stock heads, and ported manifolds with a high flow exhaust system like the Borla exhaust.  <P>The Wolverine Blue Racer made 151 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 165-ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 rpm. With the turbo it made 236 horsepower @ 6500 rpm and 210- ft. lbs. of torque @ 5000 rpm. <P>The Crane 2030 made 155 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 179-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm. With the Turbo it made 220 horsepower @ 6500 rpm and 215-ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 rpm. <P>I like the Crane PowerMax-H- 260-2 camshaft so I included that also. <BR>The Crane Powermax-H-260-2 made 156 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 178-ft. lbs. of torque from 3500-4000 rpm.  <P>Using Dragstrip2000 I came up with numbers that you could expect for performance from these camshafts if they were used in a 5-speed fiero that weighed 2925 lbs. including the driver and you have a 6100 rpm reline.  <P>The Wolverine camshaft will propel that car to 60 mph in 7.47 seconds and run the quarter mile in 15.47 seconds @ 88.2 mph if the car is NA. With the turbo the car will go 0-60 mph in 5.7 seconds and run the quarter mile in 14 seconds @ 96.9 mph.<P>The Crane 2030 camshaft will propel that car to 60 mph in 7.05 seconds and run the quarter mile in 15.14 seconds @ 89.2 mph. With the turbo you will go 0-60 mph in 5.55 seconds and run the quarter mile in 13.85 seconds @ 97.4 mph.<P>The Crane PowerMax-H-260-2 will propel that car to 60 mph in 7.04 seconds and run the quarter mile in 15.13 seconds @ 89.3 mph. With the turbo you will go 0-60 mph in 5.55 seconds and run the quarter in 13.84 seconds @ 97.4 mph.  <P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
